{"page": 3, "segments": [{"index": 0, "text": "Theorem 3.1: f(n) = \u0398(g(n)) iff f(n) = O(g(n)) AND f(n) = \u03a9(g(n)).", "rects": [[62.25, 56.24958038330078, 464.9999084472656, 70.34957885742188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0000.wav", "duration": 8.675}, {"index": 1, "text": "Asymptotic Analogy to Real Numbers: O = \u2264, \u03a9 = \u2265, \u0398 = =, o = <, \u03c9 =\n>. Asymptotic trichotomy does NOT hold (e.g., n and n^(1+sin n) are\nincomparable).", "rects": [[62.25, 82.34723663330078, 522.6300048828125, 96.44723510742188], [62.25, 96.57688903808594, 510.5889892578125, 110.54489135742188], [62.25, 110.54563903808594, 153.97799682617188, 124.51364135742188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0001.wav", "duration": 18.625}, {"index": 2, "text": "Properties: Transitivity, reflexivity, symmetry (\u0398 only), transpose symmetry. - Transpose symmetry: f = O(g) \u21d4 g = \u03a9(f). f = o(g) \u21d4 g = \u03c9(f). - Use in\nequations: 2n\u00b2 + 3n + 1 = \u0398(n\u00b2) means \u2203 c\u2081,c\u2082,n\u2080 with c\u2081\u00b7n\u00b2 \u2264 2n\u00b2+3n+1 \u2264\nc\u2082\u00b7n\u00b2.", "rects": [[62.25, 136.51129150390625, 528.78759765625, 150.61129760742188], [62.25, 150.60894775390625, 510.4526672363281, 164.70895385742188], [62.25, 164.70660400390625, 521.9136962890625, 178.80661010742188], [62.25, 178.93626403808594, 93.9540023803711, 192.90426635742188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0002.wav", "duration": 28.55}, {"index": 3, "text": "- Multiple variables: f(m,n) = O(g(m,n)) if \u2203 c,m\u2080,n\u2080 with f(m,n) \u2264\nc\u00b7g(m,n) for all m\u2265m\u2080,n\u2265n\u2080.", "rects": [[97.77000427246094, 178.93626403808594, 503.4347839355469, 192.90426635742188], [62.25, 192.90501403808594, 232.00198364257812, 206.87301635742188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0003.wav", "duration": 15.3}, {"index": 4, "text": "Limits and Asymptotics: - If lim_{n\u2192\u221e} f(n)/g(n) = 0 \u2192 f = o(g) - If\nlim_{n\u2192\u221e} f(n)/g(n) = c > 0 \u2192 f = \u0398(g) - If lim_{n\u2192\u221e} f(n)/g(n) = \u221e \u2192 f =\n\u03c9(g) - L\u2019H\u00f4pital\u2019s rule: lim f/g = lim f\u2032/g\u2032 when limits exist.", "rects": [[62.25, 218.87066650390625, 481.1368713378906, 232.97067260742188], [62.25, 232.97142028808594, 511.55413818359375, 246.93942260742188], [62.25, 246.94017028808594, 412.6260070800781, 260.9081726074219]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0004.wav", "duration": 26.5}, {"index": 5, "text": "Standard Function Growth: - Constant functions: f(n) = c \u2192 \u0398(1) < \u0398(lg\nn) - Logarithmic: lg\u2071 n, i \u2208 \u2115. All logarithms are \u0398 of each other: log_a n =\n\u0398(log_b n) for a,b>1. - Polylog vs polynomial: lg^b n = o(n^a) for any\na>0, b>0. - Polynomial vs exponential: n^b = o(a^n) for any a>1, b>0.", "rects": [[62.25, 272.90582275390625, 527.3331909179688, 287.0058288574219], [62.25, 287.135498046875, 521.3663940429688, 301.1034851074219], [62.25, 301.233154296875, 502.36676025390625, 315.2011413574219], [62.25, 315.330810546875, 515.6296997070312, 329.2987976074219]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0005.wav", "duration": 28.7}, {"index": 6, "text": "- \nFactorial: n! = \u03c9(2^n) and n! = o(n^n). - Growth order: 1 \u227a lg n \u227a \u221an \u227a n\n\u227a n lg n \u227a n\u221an \u227a n\u00b2 \u227a n\u00b3 \u227a 2\u207f \u227a n!", "rects": [[519.4457397460938, 315.330810546875, 527.3176879882812, 329.2987976074219], [62.25, 329.29644775390625, 527.38427734375, 343.3964538574219], [62.25, 343.397216796875, 272.7300720214844, 357.3652038574219]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0006.wav", "duration": 12.325}, {"index": 7, "text": "- Polynomial: p(n) = \u0398(n^d) (leading\nterm) - Exponentials (a>1) grow faster than any polynomial: lim n^b / a^n =\n0 - Polynomials grow faster than polylogs: lim lg^b n / n^a = 0 - Stirling\u2019s\napproximation: n!", "rects": [[276.54608154296875, 343.397216796875, 499.5180358886719, 357.3652038574219], [62.25, 357.365966796875, 532.3383178710938, 371.3339538574219], [62.25, 371.334716796875, 514.6022338867188, 385.3027038574219], [62.25, 385.303466796875, 170.88600158691406, 399.2714538574219]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0007.wav", "duration": 19.45}, {"index": 8, "text": "= \u221a(2\u03c0n)(n/e)^n (1 + \u0398(1/n)) - Iterated logarithm lg* n:\nmin{i \u2265 0: lg^(i) n \u2264 1} - Fibonacci: F_i = \u230a\u03d5^i/\u221a5 + 1/2\u230b, \u03d5 = (1+\u221a5)/2 \u2248\n1.618", "rects": [[174.70199584960938, 385.303466796875, 512.93408203125, 399.2714538574219], [62.25, 399.272216796875, 512.8861694335938, 413.2402038574219], [62.25, 413.240966796875, 96.59400939941406, 427.2089538574219]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0008.wav", "duration": 24.425}, {"index": 9, "text": "Pitfalls: O(n\u00b2) \u2260 \u0398(n\u00b2); saying \u201cinsertion sort running time is \u0398(n\u00b2)\u201d is wrong\n(best case \u0398(n)); asymptotic notation in inductive hypothesis without explicit\nconstants leads to false proofs.", "rects": [[62.25, 439.20660400390625, 533.0056762695312, 453.3066101074219], [62.25, 453.307373046875, 531.0301513671875, 467.2753601074219], [62.25, 467.276123046875, 250.97401428222656, 481.2441101074219]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0009.wav", "duration": 16.0}, {"index": 10, "text": "End-of-Chapter: Exercises 3.1-1 through 3.3-9; Problems 3-1 through 3-7.", "rects": [[62.25, 493.24176025390625, 520.5925903320312, 507.3417663574219]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0010.wav", "duration": 6.975}, {"index": 11, "text": "Ch. 4 \u2014 Divide-and-Conquer", "rects": [[62.25, 534.8793334960938, 284.5982360839844, 551.3760986328125]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0011.wav", "duration": 2.525}, {"index": 12, "text": "Recurrence Solving Methods", "rects": [[62.25, 565.41357421875, 256.3860168457031, 579.5135498046875]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0012.wav", "duration": 2.075}, {"index": 13, "text": "1. Substitution Method: Guess solution, prove by induction. Key: use\nexplicit constants, subtract lower-order term if proof fails.", "rects": [[62.25, 591.51123046875, 495.997314453125, 605.6112060546875], [62.25, 605.6119995117188, 417.3060607910156, 619.5799560546875]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0013.wav", "duration": 9.7}, {"index": 14, "text": "2. Recursion-Tree Method: Draw tree with costs at nodes, sum per level,\nsum across levels. Best for generating guesses.", "rects": [[62.25, 631.57763671875, 518.9915161132812, 645.6776123046875], [62.25, 645.6784057617188, 350.9700622558594, 659.6463623046875]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0014.wav", "duration": 8.45}, {"index": 15, "text": "3.", "rects": [[126.36600494384766, 56.24958038330078, 138.8939971923828, 70.34957885742188], [235.17237854003906, 493.373779296875, 246.62037658691406, 507.3417663574219], [322.22039794921875, 493.373779296875, 333.66839599609375, 507.3417663574219], [62.25, 671.64404296875, 74.77800750732422, 685.7440185546875]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0015.wav", "duration": 1.325}, {"index": 16, "text": "Master Method: For T(n) = aT(n/b) + f(n), a > 0, b > 1: | Case |\nCondition | Solution | |\u2014\u2014|\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2013|\u2014\u2014\u2014-| | 1 | f(n) = O(n^{log_b a - \u03b5}) |\nT(n) = \u0398(n^{log_b a}) | | 2 | f(n) = \u0398(n^{log_b a} lg^k n) | T(n) =\n\u0398(n^{log_b a} lg^{k+1} n) | | 3 | f(n) = \u03a9(n^{log_b a + \u03b5}) AND af(n/b) \u2264\ncf(n) for c < 1 | T(n) = \u0398(f(n)) |", "rects": [[78.9540023803711, 671.64404296875, 474.2154541015625, 685.7440185546875], [62.25, 685.7448120117188, 509.33416748046875, 699.7127685546875], [62.25, 699.7135620117188, 469.2180480957031, 713.6815185546875], [62.25, 713.6823120117188, 523.4581909179688, 727.6502685546875], [62.25, 727.6510620117188, 250.614013671875, 741.6190185546875]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0016.wav", "duration": 32.7}, {"index": 17, "text": "Watershed function: n^{log_b a}. Case 1: leaves dominate. Case 2: tied.\nCase 3: root dominates.", "rects": [[62.25, 753.6198120117188, 504.58209228515625, 767.5877685546875], [62.25, 767.5885009765625, 206.87400817871094, 781.5564575195312]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/ac17fccd/pages/3/audio/seg_0017.wav", "duration": 8.4}], "total_segments": 18, "status": "ready"}